    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "Implement a numerical experiment to test the hypothesis that small feedforward networks exhibit solution space rigidity (N_c(w) remains bounded as w increases). Design a family of analytic constraints (e.g., polynomial or trigonometric functions), train small MLPs with varying hidden widths, measure the minimum width N_c required to achieve zero violation (max absolute error ≤ 1e-3) on held-out constraints, and verify whether N_c plateaus as w grows. Use symbolic_math_tool to define constraint functions and generate data, then train networks using a lightweight framework (e.g., PyTorch or JAX) with controlled hyperparameters. Ensure reproducibility and report N_c(w) trends explicitly."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "None (custom ML experiment)"
    },
    {
